  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 300 PM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nThe upper level low will transition northeast into the eastern \nDakotas Monday night. This will lead to drier conditions on \nTuesday. On Tuesday night, a secondary shortwave trough crosses \nthe central Rockies into the Dakotas. This may bring a chance \nfor precipitation mainly to the eastern half of the state. Based\non the forecast trajectory of the shortwave, the western half \nof the state would see mainly dry conditions with this system. \nCurrently the latest deterministic GFS and EC solns do have some\nminor differences in the track of this midweek system and the \nEC would favor a more westward extent to precipitation chances. \nFor now, given the differences, the latest WPC forecast seems on\ntrack. Wednesday and Thursday appear dry and seasonal ATTM with\nanother trough deepening across the western CONUS late next \nweek. This could lead to an active pattern across the central \nCONUS next weekend.",
